Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• BADGES."class": distinguishes badge class (gold/silver/bronze). We will filter to gold, e.g. WHERE "class" = 1.  
• BADGES."name": the badge’s text; used for grouping and display.  
• BADGES."user_id": lets us connect a badge to a user and find the user’s first‑ever gold badge.  
• BADGES."date": the moment the badge was awarded; needed to detect which gold badge came first and how long after sign‑up it was earned.  
• USERS."id": primary key to join with BADGES."user_id".  
• USERS."creation_date": the user’s account creation moment; used to compute the interval (badge date – creation date).  

Typical filter / join conditions  
• BADGES."class" = 1                        -- keep only gold badges  
• BADGES."user_id" = USERS."id"             -- join badges to their owners  
• BADGES."date" = MIN(BADGES."date") …      -- isolate the first gold badge per user  
• QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() … = 1                -- alternate way to pick the first gold badge in Snowflake  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows where applicable).  
All identifiers are quoted; adjust DATABASE / SCHEMA / TABLE names if different in your system.

```sql
-- 1) Preview a handful of badge records
SELECT
  "id",
  "user_id",
  "name",
  "class",
  "date"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) How many badges exist in each class? (helps confirm which number = gold)
SELECT
  "class",
  COUNT(*) AS "badge_count"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
GROUP BY "class"
ORDER BY "class";
```

```sql
-- 3) Distinct gold‑badge names (first 20)
SELECT DISTINCT
  "name"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE "class" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Join badges to their owners and show the raw time difference
SELECT
  b."id"           AS "badge_id",
  b."name"         AS "badge_name",
  b."date"         AS "badge_date",
  u."creation_date",
  (b."date" - u."creation_date") AS "microseconds_between"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"  b
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"   u
  ON b."user_id" = u."id"
WHERE b."class" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) First gold‑badge date for each user
SELECT
  "user_id",
  MIN("date") AS "first_gold_date"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
WHERE "class" = 1
GROUP BY "user_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) First gold‑badge name per user (sub‑query version)
WITH first_gold AS (
  SELECT
    "user_id",
    MIN("date") AS "first_gold_date"
  FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
  WHERE "class" = 1
  GROUP BY "user_id"
)
SELECT
  fg."user_id",
  b."name",
  b."date"
FROM first_gold fg
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
  ON b."user_id" = fg."user_id"
 AND b."date"    = fg."first_gold_date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Count how many users share the same first gold badge
WITH first_gold AS (
  SELECT
    "user_id",
    MIN("date") AS "first_gold_date"
  FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
  WHERE "class" = 1
  GROUP BY "user_id"
)
SELECT
  b."name"                     AS "badge_name",
  COUNT(*)                     AS "user_count"
FROM first_gold fg
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
  ON b."user_id" = fg."user_id"
 AND b."date"    = fg."first_gold_date"
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "user_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Add average days from sign‑up to first gold badge
WITH first_gold AS (
  SELECT
    "user_id",
    MIN("date") AS "first_gold_date"
  FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES"
  WHERE "class" = 1
  GROUP BY "user_id"
)
SELECT
  b."name" AS "badge_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "user_count",
  AVG( (b."date" - u."creation_date") / (86400*1000000.0) ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM first_gold fg
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
  ON b."user_id" = fg."user_id"
 AND b."date"    = fg."first_gold_date"
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS" u
  ON u."id" = fg."user_id"
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "user_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but using QUALIFY instead of a sub‑query
SELECT
  b."name" AS "badge_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "user_count",
  AVG( (b."date" - u."creation_date") / (86400*1000000.0) ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS"  u
  ON u."id" = b."user_id"
WHERE b."class" = 1
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id" ORDER BY b."date") = 1
GROUP BY b."name"
ORDER BY "user_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Final query: top 10 gold badges most commonly earned first, with counts and average days
WITH first_gold AS (
  SELECT
    b."user_id",
    b."name",
    b."date"
  FROM "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."BADGES" b
  WHERE b."class" = 1
  QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY b."user_id" ORDER BY b."date") = 1
)
SELECT
  fg."name" AS "badge_name",
  COUNT(*)  AS "users_first_badge",
  AVG( (fg."date" - u."creation_date") / (86400*1000000.0) ) AS "avg_days_to_badge"
FROM first_gold fg
JOIN "STACKOVERFLOW"."STACKOVERFLOW"."USERS" u
  ON u."id" = fg."user_id"
GROUP BY fg."name"
ORDER BY "users_first_badge" DESC
LIMIT 10;
```
